1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,034
VendorLink.

2
00:00:01,034 --> 00:00:09,183
AI agents that let small makers sell to modern retailers: in their own language, within rules they set, with every action provable.

3
00:00:09,721 --> 00:00:11,097
Both sides want the sale.

4
00:00:11,097 --> 00:00:17,592
Home makers make what local shoppers search for, but retail runs on English forms, catalogue standards and fine print.

5
00:00:17,592 --> 00:00:23,756
And a maker who supplies forty a day costs a buyer as much work as a big distributor, so the sale never happens.

6
00:00:26,066 --> 00:00:30,061
VendorLink gives every maker an agent, and keeps every agent honest.

7
00:00:30,061 --> 00:00:36,170
Maya's Concierge talks with her, and her Guardian, plain code with no model, is the only one that signs.

8
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:39,519
FreshCart's orchestrator hands work to specialist agents.

9
00:00:39,519 --> 00:00:45,511
Between them, a trust gateway checks identity, permission and content, and keeps a tamper-evident log.

10
00:00:47,825 --> 00:00:48,387
Meet Maya.

11
00:00:48,387 --> 00:00:50,578
She pours candles at home in Hyderabad.

12
00:00:50,578 --> 00:00:57,095
To list a product, she sends a phone photo and a few words: forty lavender candles at two hundred and twenty rupees.

13
00:00:59,235 --> 00:01:04,693
The retailer's agents check the photo against catalogue standards: too small, cluttered background.

14
00:01:04,693 --> 00:01:13,018
They make an auto-enhanced version and two AI versions of her own photo, and write the title and description from her words, each fact with its source.

15
00:01:13,018 --> 00:01:16,656
Her Guardian never approves an AI photo for her, so she picks one.

16
00:01:18,514 --> 00:01:21,449
FreshCart's policy sends AI photos to a person.

17
00:01:21,449 --> 00:01:29,068
The category manager sees her photo beside the AI one, with every flag in words, and publishes it, the AI photo disclosed.

18
00:01:30,736 --> 00:01:37,798
Maya set her rules once: at least one hundred and eighty rupees a candle, forty a day, pickup after ten, paid within fifteen days.

19
00:01:37,798 --> 00:01:40,786
Her Guardian keeps them as her signed standing mandate.

20
00:01:43,986 --> 00:01:50,823
FreshCart's gifting desk orders fifty candles at two hundred and twenty rupees, pickup at eight in the morning, paid in forty-five days.

21
00:01:52,545 --> 00:01:56,546
Her Guardian checks it in plain code, in under a millisecond.

22
00:01:56,546 --> 00:01:59,169
Red: too many, too early, paid too late.

23
00:01:59,169 --> 00:02:03,628
It counters inside her rules: forty candles, ten a.m., fifteen days.

24
00:02:04,918 --> 00:02:10,230
The counter changes the order value by twenty percent, and FreshCart auto-accepts only ten.

25
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:14,199
So the buyer is asked, with the reasons in words, here and on Slack.

26
00:02:14,199 --> 00:02:16,884
Whichever answer comes first closes the other.

27
00:02:16,884 --> 00:02:17,934
The buyer accepts.

28
00:02:19,436 --> 00:02:24,964
The deal is amber: inside her rules, but over her auto-accept limit, so it waits for Maya.

29
00:02:24,964 --> 00:02:29,877
Her app and read-backs work in Telugu or Bahasa Indonesia; we show English here.

30
00:02:29,877 --> 00:02:34,053
Her own yes is the consent, bound to the hash of this exact version.

31
00:02:34,931 --> 00:02:39,773
Her Guardian signs, FreshCart countersigns, and the gateway files the order mandate.

32
00:02:39,773 --> 00:02:41,849
No model decided or signed anything.

33
00:02:43,542 --> 00:02:52,060
Operators see every agent: who talks to whom, trust scores, every decision, and how long each step takes and how many tokens it used.

34
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:55,326
Any agent can be suspended, quarantined or revoked.

35
00:02:56,504 --> 00:03:02,343
Now an attack: an impostor without Maya's key, and a document with hidden instructions for the model.

36
00:03:02,343 --> 00:03:05,408
The gateway blocks both and quarantines the uploader.

37
00:03:05,408 --> 00:03:07,200
Maya's real agent is untouched.

38
00:03:08,039 --> 00:03:10,530
A new market is configuration, not code.

39
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:18,936
One click switches FreshCart to packaged food in Indonesia: Bahasa, rupiah, local food-safety permits, and different specialist agents.

40
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:26,221
Sara's cassava chips label has no P-IRT registration number, so the Label Checker flags it before anything is listed.

41
00:03:28,474 --> 00:03:30,122
And everything is provable.

42
00:03:30,122 --> 00:03:32,501
Verify replays the audit chain: intact.

43
00:03:32,501 --> 00:03:36,162
Tamper with one record, and it breaks at exactly that entry.

44
00:03:36,997 --> 00:03:37,812
VendorLink.

45
00:03:37,812 --> 00:03:44,482
Agents for small makers: in their language, inside their rules, with trust you can verify.

46
00:03:44,482 --> 00:03:48,780
Built with Gemini, the Agent Development Kit, A2A and MCP.
